            "paragraph_1": "<p>This one surprises people the most.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "<p>Parasites feed on simple sugars. When they’re present in your gut, they send signals that drive cravings not because you lack willpower, but because <strong>something else in your gut is hungry too.</strong></p>",
            "paragraph_3": "<p><strong>Sea Moss and Moringa</strong> rebuild the gut lining those organisms damage, while the formula’s other botanicals target the organisms directly. Most people notice cravings ease by week two.</p>",
            "background_color": "#224b38",
            "text_color": "#ffffff",
            "vertical_padding": 30,
            "heading_size": 24,
            "text_size": 16,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "listicle3section3_di4kxJ": {
          "type": "listicle3section3",
          "name": "Blog split layout343",
          "settings": {
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "padding_vertical": 5,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "<p>4. Your belly won’t move no matter how clean you eat</p>",
            "heading_size": 28,
            "paragraph_1": "<p>Toxic waste buildup in the colon doesn’t just sit there passively  it produces inflammatory byproducts that signal your body to hold onto fat as a protective response.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "<p><strong>You’re not failing at your diet. Your gut is working against it.</strong></p>",
            "paragraph_3": "<p><strong>Senna and Turmeric</strong> in Rootvana’s formula support the elimination process that clears this buildup, while reducing the inflammation driving the fat storage response.</p>",
            "paragraph_size": 16,
            "text_gap": 0,
            "paragraph_gap": 0,
