            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "vertical_padding": 20,
            "image_max_width": 300,
            "image_border_color": "#ffffff",
            "heading": "<p>1. No More Blood Donations</p>",
            "heading_size": 32,
            "paragraph_1": "<p>Most men on TRT end up in a donation chair every 8 to 12 weeks trying to keep their hematocrit down. Hemo Flow manages blood viscosity daily so your numbers stay in range without the donations, the iron crashes, and the exhaustion that comes with them.</p>",
            "paragraph_2": "",
